From: Michael-CY Lee <michael-cy.lee@mediatek.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Oct 2024 14:50:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mtk: hostapd: clear authroized flag when removing STA from the
 driver during association handling

When removing the STA from the driver, authorized flag should be cleared
at the same time. Failing to do so may result in the STA being re-added
with authorized flag enabled.

Link: https://github.com/mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds/blob/08196fa6e5d338ce88aa0002f781e2d24289b1f1/autobuild/unified/filogic/mac80211/25.12/files/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/0111-mtk-hostapd-clear-authroized-flag-when-removing-STA-.patch
Signed-off-by: Michael-CY Lee <michael-cy.lee@mediatek.com>
[plcharriere: clear it with ap_sta_set_authorized() before the driver
entry is removed, as ap_sta_re_add() does, instead of with
ap_sta_set_authorized_flag() after it, so that the change is reported
like any other and a later disconnect is not lost]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 src/ap/ieee802_11.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -6708,6 +6708,7 @@ static int add_associated_sta(struct hostapd_data *hap
 	     (!wpa_auth_sta_ft_tk_already_set(sta->wpa_sm) &&
 	      !wpa_auth_sta_fils_tk_already_set(sta->wpa_sm)) ||
 	     (!reassoc && (sta->flags & WLAN_STA_AUTHORIZED)))) {
+		ap_sta_set_authorized(hapd, sta, 0);
 		hostapd_drv_sta_remove(hapd, sta->addr);
 		wpa_auth_sm_event(sta->wpa_sm, WPA_DRV_STA_REMOVED);
 		set = 0;
